WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:03.810
Which is the real you?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.650
Is that what you're worried about?

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.490
Hiding your true self...

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.990
Deceiving the people around you...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.110
Doesn't it hurt, Sempai?

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:22.090
"Sempai"? You're acting like you're the same.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.090
Anybody who's tricked by those, it's their own fault.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:09.060
Aria of a Pounding Heart

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.080
Sasaki, thanks for this.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.430
You could've just given it back during club meetings.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:17.440
Or you're not going right now, right?

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.250
What's up, Tsuchiura?

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.990
No, it's nothing.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:25.580
Is it Hino?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.100
She's in this class, after all.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.700
So are you two dating like they say?

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:35.110
What? Like who says? Geez...

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.540
Bye.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.100
You're coming back, right?

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:48.320
Hey, Sasaki!

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.940
Right, I'll be right there.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.310
Peace.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.570
Come back...

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.820
which was I thinking about just now?

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.260
I was late getting here, I guess...

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.760
I wonder if there's any melon bread left.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.020
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.020
No, I'm sorry.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.440
Kaho-sempai?

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.720
Oh, Fuyuumi-chan!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.740
It sure is crowded.

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.100
What are you coming to buy?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.090
Some lead for my mechanical pencil... but...

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.990
OK, let's charge in together!

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.940
Kaho-sempai?

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.140
Fuyuumi-chan!

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:52.750
Are you OK, Fuyuumi-chan?

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:56.590
Yes, I managed to buy my lead, somehow.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:01.720
Um, Kaho-sempai, I'm sorry about yesterday.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.430
About the song for the third selection...

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:09.190
No, it's nothing for you to apologize about.

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:12.560
But anyway, Amo-san sure is mature.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:18.050
What's more, you have to decide the song you're going to play or there's no point, is there?

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.710
To be honest, those words really struck me.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:29.300
Yes... when I heard them, I thought to myself that playing an instrument means facing oneself.

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:33.200
But I just can't decide on a song.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:39.530
I'm sure you'll find one. Something irreplaceable to you.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:43.130
Kaho-sempai... right!

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.920
Want to use it? Just opened up.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:57.690
Thanks; I've got another room reserved.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:05:03.160
Anyway, about yesterday... I don't want you to say things that invite misunderstandings.

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:05.490
What, yesterday?

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.950
Then are you that guy's girlfriend?

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.920
Is that really that important enough to drag up?

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.620
It was just a minor misunderstanding.

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:17.040
Explain to your girlfriend the situation, please.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.040
And you need to not get the wrong idea yourself.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.520
She's not my girlfriend at all anymore.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.340
Is that really that important?

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.290
Hey...

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:30.770
There you are you, two.

00:05:30.770 --> 00:05:35.880
Kanayan said there's going to be a meeting about the third selection, so come to the conference room.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:41.060
It's no good.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:45.670
Neither Fuyuumi-chan nor I have anything we can give you.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.200
Stingy...

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.940
What are you doing here anyway?

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.420
Don't worry about it.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:58.320
Anyway, I've been wanting to ask just you girls, how are those five, normally?

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.390
They're all popular with the girls, aren't they?

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:06.510
I don't know what you mean by "Usually"...

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:09.580
Then just tell me which is your type?

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:13.500
There's rumors about you and Tsuchiura-kun you know...

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.270
Oh, you're all here already.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.260
That was fast.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.620
You were called too, Mori-san?

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:22.760
That's right.

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:27.790
I know! Mori-san's likely to be more familiar with the four in the Music Department.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:30.240
How are they like, usually?

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.830
Usually, huh?

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:39.070
I'm in Tsukimori-kun's class, and he's amazing with the violin, and so cute too, right?

00:06:39.070 --> 00:06:41.480
Lots of girls really like him.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.380
I knew it!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.560
But with his personality being what it is he doesn't have many friends.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.640
Well, he's not too friendly.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.220
I guess the nice way of putting it is "cool".

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:58.510
But he could be a bit more friendly, couldn't he?

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:02.070
That's true... like Hihara-sempai?

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.060
Then he'd be a totally different person.

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:08.610
It would be even harder to talk to him!

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:13.990
I think as he is he's going to find life pretty hard. As a person...

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:18.090
That's right, I know what you mean. He'll lead a hard life.

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:18.090
Um, I don't think we need to worry about him that much...

00:07:18.090 --> 00:07:19.800
I think that's a bit much for us to say.

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:21.130
Then what about Hihara-sempai?

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:22.410
Hihara-sempai?

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.580
They're not listening.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.420
Come to think of it, a bit ago...

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.080
Hihara-sempai...

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.700
You dropped this.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:34.770
Sorry, thank you!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.370
Hihara-sempai really is cute!

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:39.520
Right?

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:41.120
Is what happened?

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:48.850
Huh? Is that really worth the whole "Oh Hihara-sempai is so wonderful" thing?

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:51.060
You're right, just being cute isn't good enough.

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:53.710
I think here the best option is...

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.620
Sorry, thank you!

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:02.070
Yunoki-sama!

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.050
The ideal option?

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:06.880
He's not really my type...

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:09.740
Yeah, not mine either.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.130
And that leaves Shimizu-kun.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:18.400
Thank... you... sempai.

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:21.650
Isn't that so awesome?

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:23.060
I understand, I really do!

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:26.020
He's the best! Hiba-kohai!

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:28.530
They're dangerous, lets stay away from them Fuyuumi-chan.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:29.660
Yes.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.040
It's hard to go in...

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:39.540
Come to think of it, something just like this happened a while ago.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:42.500
You dropped this, Tsuchiura-kun.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.840
Oh, sorry. Thanks a ton.

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:49.130
He's actually nice in a quiet way, Shimizu-kun.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.440
What, what?

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.620
You were thinking of somebody, weren't you?

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.000
N-Not really!

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:58.350
Come to think of it, have you heard about the violin romance?

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.030
The love born between two rivals for the competition!

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.650
A miracle romance!

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.200
But that was a long time ago wasn't it?

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:11.420
So like I was saying; it might happen for the first time in 25 years!

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:13.610
Hino-san plays the violin after all.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.570
So who do you like the most?

00:09:19.190 --> 00:09:22.720
What are you doing, everybody? Standing outside the door.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:25.400
Yunoki-sempai! You scared me!

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:30.490
Wow, listening in. You guys suck.

00:09:30.490 --> 00:09:33.300
It's because you guys made it impossible to go in!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.340
Oh my.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:46.780
Vacation days are the perfect chance to practice in front of others...

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:48.830
But maybe I'd be in the way here?

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.990
Basketball, huh?

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:56.320
They look like they're having fun.

00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.570
All right!

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.650
Hihara-sempai!

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.490
Hino-chan?

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:07.870
What's up, Hino-chan?

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.510
Practicing?

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:14.220
Yeah, I can't do it at home, so I thought I'd do it at the park...

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.420
Kazuki, she a classmate?

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:19.690
Yeah bro, she's a sophomore, her name is Hino-chan.

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.730
Hi, I'm his older brother, Haruki.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.390
He's probably always causing problems for you.

00:10:25.390 --> 00:10:26.240
Sorry.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.620
No, not at all.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.660
Don't be a jerk, bro!

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:33.260
Kazuki's kohai, huh?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.800
Cute, isn't she?

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.610
I'm Yamaguchi. Hi.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.320
Hey, want to hang out with us for a bit?

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:41.070
Wait, everybody.

00:10:41.070 --> 00:10:42.320
We're kidding.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.140
Sorry, Hino-chan.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:47.450
Don't worry about me, play your game.

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:48.570
OK.

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:51.630
Um, can I practice here?

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.640
Yeah.

00:10:53.640 --> 00:10:56.050
But say so when you want to go home, OK?

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:56.950
Sure.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.070
Now to practice...

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:20.940
What's wrong, Kazuki?

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.630
I should've brought my trumpet.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.920
Nothing.

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:27.310
What are you doing?

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:36.370
Money!

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:41.060
It's been a while since I've played in a such a relaxed way.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.720
Everybody's been so weird lately.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:51.610
Hino-chan?

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:53.930
Sorry, it's nothing.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.580
That was a coincidence.

00:12:03.680 --> 00:12:06.280
Are you Ryotaro's girlfriend?

00:12:09.410 --> 00:12:11.890
Hino-chan, what's wrong?

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:13.160
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:17.010
Kazuki, I remembered I have something to do, I'm heading out.

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:18.560
Me too.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:19.380
Bye!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:22.340
The game's not over yet!

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:24.370
That hat...

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:28.550
Thank her for the hat, would you?

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:52.400
Sempai, I can pay for my myself.

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:54.110
Come on, come on.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:58.140
You helped me pick out a present, and I never thanked you properly.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:04.300
Hino-san?

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:05.760
Tsuchiura?

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.320
Hino... Hihara-sempai?

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:11.390
So you're her real boyfriend, right?

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:15.060
Boyfriend?! No, well...

00:13:16.150 --> 00:13:19.280
I'm sorry. I did it again, didn't I?

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:23.460
But the second I saw you, I thought you looked great together.

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:25.450
Looked great?

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.450
I'm Mizue Sakimoto.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:30.400
Ryotaro's ex-girlfriend.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:33.050
Tsuchiura's ex-girlfriend?

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:37.370
Yeah, for a bit when I was in middle school...

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:39.310
Wow, an ex-girlfriend!

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:41.880
So you have had a girlfriend!

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:44.610
Hihara-sempai?

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.220
You're his sempai?

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:49.240
Yeah, I'm in third year, my name is Kazuki Hihara.

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:51.820
Are you on the soccer team too?

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:53.770
No, I'm in the Oke club.

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:54.660
Oke club?

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:57.180
The Orchestra club!

00:13:57.180 --> 00:14:00.140
I play the trumpet!

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:01.910
The trumpet?

00:14:01.910 --> 00:14:04.310
You can play an instrument? How wonderful!

00:14:04.310 --> 00:14:06.190
Not at all!

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:09.620
Hino-chan's in General Studies, and she's great with the violin.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:10.810
She plays the violin?

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:13.380
And Tsuchiura is great with the piano.

00:14:13.380 --> 00:14:14.760
Piano?

00:14:14.760 --> 00:14:17.520
They're good enough to be in the school-wide Competition.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:20.880
Tsuchiura and the two of us are all participating in it.

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:23.750
Amazing, Ryotaro!

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.710
But you're in General Studies, huh?

00:14:26.710 --> 00:14:29.420
Yeah, but some stuff happened.

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:32.260
Yeah, that surprised me!

00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:37.510
He just got up on stage and accompanied Hino-chan's performance!

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.910
You practicing, Hino?

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:50.360
Yeah, ever since you suggested it, I've been doing it at the park on my days off.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:52.880
I see. You're working hard.

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:55.500
Were you practicing with Hihara-san?

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:59.540
No. I just happened to see him and his brother playing basketball...

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:04.660
My brother and his friends said they had something to do and left, so we came to get some tea.

00:15:04.660 --> 00:15:06.320
Basketball, huh?

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:11.150
By the way, Ryotaro, you were really good at basketball, not just soccer, weren't you?

00:15:11.150 --> 00:15:12.160
Yeah?

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:16.890
Yeah! In gym all the girls were like "He's so cool!" and stuff.

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:17.830
You didn't know?

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.310
Of course not.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:21.410
Geez, Ryotaro is so straight-laced.

00:15:21.410 --> 00:15:24.680
But that was what I liked about him.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:28.820
I've never seen Tsuchiura-kun like this, I don't think...

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:38.730
She's cute, very feminine...

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:46.420
Hey, Hino-san, don't you want to see them play one another?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.430
Why did this happen?

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.820
I sometimes play basketball with my friends in General Studies,

00:15:58.820 --> 00:16:00.560
but I've never played basketball with you.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:03.520
I've never played it outside of school.

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.150
Oh, I see.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:07.250
It'd be bad if you hurt your fingers or something, wouldn't it?

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.690
I won't screw up like that.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.470
Amazing!

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:20.780
Now it's my turn!

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.680
Hiharu-san is so cool!

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:44.910
Don't you agree, Hino-san?

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:46.590
Yeah...

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.950
Our second year in middle school...

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:03.910
I confessed my feelings to him.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:07.460
But we broke up after three months.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.740
I was the one who suggested it.

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:36.210
Back then, he looked like he was having lots of fun when he was with his guy friends,

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:40.360
but he never seemed to be having fun with me.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:45.220
I wanted him to call me by my name, Mizue.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:50.160
I always wanted my boyfriend to call me that.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:55.020
But he never did.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:59.790
Come to think of it, I just wanted to be in love with somebody.

00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:02.460
I was such a kid.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:06.270
There's nothing between me and him now.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:11.740
We just happened to meet at the station for the first time in a while, and I just invited him for tea for old times sake.

00:18:11.740 --> 00:18:14.310
He should've just refused...

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.270
But he's kind in the weirdest way.

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:22.040
Which are you really after?

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:22.950
Huh?

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.260
Ryotaro?

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:25.490
Hihara-san?

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:27.780
Or the one you were with at the station?

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:33.670
Hihara-sempai?

00:18:35.680 --> 00:18:37.400
Ow...

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.920
Are you OK, Hihara-sempai?

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.630
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.850
You're bleeding!

00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:46.440
Don't worry, I'll just put some spit on it and it'll heal.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:47.670
But...

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:53.110
I'm heading back. Escort me, OK?

00:18:55.010 --> 00:18:57.800
OK, I'll be leaving.

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:00.810
Oh, good luck in the competition!

00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:02.730
Bye!

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:19.170
You thinking about the two of them?

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:24.020
I never knew you could play the piano.

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:31.270
You're much softer than you were back then. Whose fault is that, I wonder?

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:34.350
Thanks for walking me this far.

00:19:34.350 --> 00:19:35.750
Bye!

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:42.160
Whose fault?

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:46.930
It's fine, it's fine... it's not that big a deal.

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.080
No!

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:50.430
What if it gets infected?

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:57.090
You may think its just a scrape, but what if it affects your performance?

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:02.340
What's wrong, Sempai?

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.180
Nothing!

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:10.640
There we are. Put out your arm.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:12.720
OK.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.990
There we go.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:21.530
It's kind of silly looking, but put up with it, OK?

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:23.700
Kaho-chan...

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:29.180
This is much cuter, I think.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:33.630
Yeah, it's cute isn't it? "Kaho-chan".

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:36.090
Do you mind?

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:39.040
No, I don't, but...

00:20:39.040 --> 00:20:42.540
Then you can call me Kazuki-sempai.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.250
I wanted him to call me by my name.

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:50.300
I'll pass.

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:52.100
Y-Yeah?

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:54.320
OK, let's go home.

00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:56.240
The sun's going to set.

00:20:58.370 --> 00:20:59.720
Kaho-chan.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:05.580
Hihara-sempai, what's wrong?

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:12.440
Oh, I see.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.410
I like her.

00:23:36.230 --> 00:23:39.740
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:45.290
The great composers displayed their musical passion in the expression of a love between a man and his wife.

00:23:45.290 --> 00:23:51.370
Schumann's "Piano Sonata #1" and Elgar's "Salut d'amour" were both composed for and dedicated to their beloved wives.

00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:58.230
And for his wife's birthday, Wagner gathered and orchestra and performed the "Siegfried Idyll" for the first time.

00:23:58.230 --> 00:23:59.970
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:59.970 --> 00:24:03.640
Wagner's wife was the daughter of a famous composer.

00:24:03.640 --> 00:24:05.330
Who was he?

00:24:05.330 --> 00:24:07.050
A violin class?

00:24:07.050 --> 00:24:09.300
We're going to teach the kids?

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:10.310
Can I do that OK?

00:24:10.310 --> 00:24:12.970
Hino, what was that sound?

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:16.320
Um... well my stomach rumbled.

00:24:16.320 --> 00:24:18.370
Next episode: The Lying Violin.

00:24:18.370 --> 00:24:20.430
She's talented...

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:23.740
The answer is... Liszt!
